.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-2-Clause
.Dd August 23, 2026
.Dt SATLD 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm satld
.Nd SatL container engine daemon
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm satld
.Op Fl \-config Ar PATH
.Op Fl \-log\-format Ar text|json
.Op Fl \-log\-level Ar LEVEL
.Op Fl \-log\-target Ar stdout|syslog
.Op Fl \-metrics\-addr Ar ADDR
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is the SatL daemon: a Docker-compatible container engine and cluster
orchestrator for FreeBSD, running OCI containers as VNET jails through
the external
.Xr ocijail 1
runtime.
One
.Nm
runs per node.
It serves the Docker Engine REST API on a unix socket, the only external
surface, and an internal mTLS gRPC protocol on port 2377 for clustering.
A fresh daemon initializes a cluster of one on first start; there is no
separate init step, and a single node is simply a cluster of one.
.Pp
Startup proceeds in a fixed order: the configuration file is loaded
(a missing file means defaults, see
.Xr satld.toml 5 ) ;
the ZFS preflight runs, and the daemon refuses to start when its root
dataset is absent; host facts are gathered; the node runtime is built,
including the
.Ql satl/*
pf anchors and the devfs ruleset containers run under; the node's
identity and cluster runtime come up; startup reconciliation re-adopts
the live jails a previous daemon left running and destroys what leaked;
only then does the REST API begin answering.
.Pp
.Nm
must run as root.
ZFS is mandatory: there is no fallback storage driver.
For published ports and container egress NAT,
.Xr pf 4
must be loaded and enabled with the
.Ql satl/*
anchors declared in
.Pa /etc/pf.conf .
Resource limits (memory, cpu) additionally need the boot tunable
.Ql kern.racct.enable=1 ;
without it the daemon degrades gracefully and enforces nothing.
.Pp
The options are as follows:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl \-config Ar PATH
Path to the daemon configuration file.
The default is
.Pa /usr/local/etc/satl/satld.toml ;
a missing file means built-in defaults, a malformed one is fatal.
.It Fl \-log\-format Ar text|json
Log output format.
The default is
.Ql text .
.It Fl \-log\-level Ar LEVEL
Log level filter (default
.Ql info ) .
The
.Ev RUST_LOG
environment variable overrides this flag when set.
.It Fl \-log\-target Ar stdout|syslog
Where log lines go.
.Ql syslog
sends one datagram per event to the local syslogd and is what the rc.d
service uses;
.Ql stdout ,
the default, is for running the daemon in the foreground.
.It Fl \-metrics\-addr Ar ADDR
Address the Prometheus
.Ql /metrics
endpoint binds, overriding
.Ql metrics_addr
in the config file.
The endpoint is off unless one of the two is set, and it is
unauthenticated, like dockerd's: bind a private address.
.El
.Pp
Internal:
.Nm
re-executes itself as
.Ql satld __jail-arp ,
an in-jail ARP helper visible in
.Xr ps 1 ;
it is not an operator command.
.Ss rc.conf variables
The rc.d script
.Pa /usr/local/etc/rc.d/satld
runs the daemon under
.Xr daemon 8
and understands the following
.Xr rc.conf 5
variables:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Va satld_enable
Set to
.Ql YES
to start
.Nm
at boot (default
.Ql NO ) .
.It Va satld_config
Configuration file passed as
.Fl \-config
(default
.Pa /usr/local/etc/satl/satld.toml ) .
.It Va satld_flags
Extra
.Nm
flags, for example
.Ql \-\-log\-format json .
.It Va satld_env
Environment for the daemon, for example
.Ql RUST_LOG=satld=debug .
.El
.Pp
The script always passes
.Fl \-log\-target Cm syslog ,
and that flag is a correctness requirement, not a preference: it makes
.Nm
hand each log event to syslogd as its own datagram, one event one line.
Letting
.Xr daemon 8
forward the log instead merges events written microseconds apart onto
one line of
.Pa /var/log/messages
and loses part of a burst outright.
Do not remove it when editing
.Va command_args .
.Ss Network ports
.Bl -tag -width "4790-4999/udp" -compact
.It 2377/tcp
Internal gRPC (Raft, Control, Dispatcher, NodeCA), mTLS on every
connection.
.It 2378/tcp
NodeCA bootstrap for joining nodes, unauthenticated by design: a joiner
has no certificate yet and pins the CA against the digest in its join
token.
Always the internal gRPC listen port plus one.
.It 4789/udp
VXLAN overlay networks.
.It 4790-4999/udp
Encrypted overlay networks; each one gets its own VTEP port from this
range, carried inside ESP (IP protocol 50) between nodes.
.El
.Sh SIGNALS
.Nm
shuts down cleanly on
.Dv SIGTERM
and
.Dv SIGINT .
Running jails deliberately survive the daemon: containers keep running
across a stop or an upgrade and are re-adopted by the next start's
reconciliation pass.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa /usr/local/etc/satl/satld.toml
Daemon configuration,
.Xr satld.toml 5 .
.It Pa /usr/local/etc/satl/satld.toml.sample
Installed sample listing every key and its default.
.It Pa /var/run/satl.sock
The Docker REST API unix socket.
.It Pa /var/db/satl
Node state directory, normally the mountpoint of the ZFS root dataset.
.It Pa /var/run/satld.pid
Pid file written by
.Xr daemon 8
for the rc.d service.
.It Pa /usr/local/etc/rc.d/satld
The rc.d service script.
.El
.Sh DIAGNOSTICS
Under the rc.d service the daemon logs to syslog with the tag
.Ql satld ,
which the stock
.Pa /etc/syslog.conf
lands in
.Pa /var/log/messages
and
.Pa /var/log/daemon.log .
Always read the log with
.Ql grep \-a :
a single non-ASCII byte anywhere in the file makes plain
.Xr grep 1
print nothing at all, which looks exactly like the daemon logged
nothing.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr satl 1 ,
.Xr pf 4 ,
.Xr rc.conf 5 ,
.Xr satld.toml 5 ,
.Xr daemon 8 ,
.Xr zfs 8
.Pp
.Lk https://docs.satl.cc/ "SatL manual"
